\f0\fs24 \cf0 This is arbitrary extension/application metadata.\
The crucial architectural rule is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Metadata should not become your main application payload.\
Bad:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 "metadata": \{\
   "origin": "BLR",\
   "destination": "LHR"\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 when those are actually part of the agent input.\
Better:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 parts.data\
   = semantic/business payload\
\
metadata\
   = auxiliary transport/application context\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 18. 
\f4\fs52 message.extensions
\f1\fs48 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 "extensions": [\
  "https://example.com/a2a/extensions/citations/v1"\
]\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 These identify A2A extensions applicable to the message.\
Think of them as:\
