\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 A concrete example\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Imagine your Architecture Review Agent.\
You send:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Message:\
\
"Review this architecture against our security standards."\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 The A2A server decides this requires work.\
It creates:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 taskId = task-8421\
contextId = ctx-123\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 and returns:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \{\
  "id": "task-8421",\
  "contextId": "ctx-123",\
  "status": \{\
    "state": "TASK_STATE_WORKING"\
  \}\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Now there is a persistent protocol object representing:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Architecture review #8421 is currently being executed.
\f0\b0 \
That's what the Task means.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 What can happen to this Task?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

