\f0\fs24 \cf0 So Task is essentially an 
\f1\b agent execution state machine exposed through the protocol
\f0\b0 . A2A specifically uses Tasks to represent stateful interactions and supports interrupted states such as input-required/auth-required as well as terminal states such as completed, failed, canceled, and rejected. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://a2a-protocol.org/dev/topics/life-of-a-task/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 A2A Protocol}}\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 Here's where it becomes different from chat\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Suppose the agent gets halfway through and discovers:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 I need to know which environment you want me to analyse: DEV or PROD.\
A chatbot might simply respond:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 "Which environment?"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 And now your application has to invent its own state management.\
A2A instead says:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Task task-8421\
\
status:\
    INPUT_REQUIRED\
\
message:\
    "Which environment should I analyse?"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 The Task is still alive.\
Client sends:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Message:\
    "PROD"\
\
taskId:\
    task-8421\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Now:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 task-8421\
\
INPUT_REQUIRED\
      
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2 \
      
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2  "PROD"\
      
\f3 \uc0\u9660 
\f2 \
WORKING\
      
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2 \
      
\f3 \uc0\u9660 
\f2 \
COMPLETED\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 That's considerably richer than ordinary chatbot semantics.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 This distinction is important\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Think of these three IDs separately:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 contextId\
    
\f3 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
"What's the overall conversation/business context?"\
\
taskId\
    
\f3 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
"What piece of work are we currently doing?"\
\
messageId\
    
\f3 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
"What individual communication happened?"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 contextId = architecture-session-123\
\
    
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2 \
    
\f3 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f2  task-001\
    
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2      Review security\
    
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2 \
    
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2      
\f3 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f2  msg-01 "Review security"\
    
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2      
\f3 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f2  msg-02 "Which environment?"\
    
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2      
\f3 \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472 
\f2  msg-03 "PROD"\
    
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2 \
    
\f3 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f2  task-002\
    
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2      Generate deployment architecture\
    
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2 \
    
\f3 \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472 
\f2  task-003\
          Estimate infrastructure cost\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 One 
\f1\b context
\f0\b0  can contain multiple 
\f1\b tasks
\f0\b0 , and each task can involve multiple 
\f1\b messages
\f0\b0 . A2A's current specification explicitly describes 
\f2\fs26 contextId
\f0\fs24  as grouping related tasks/messages, while 
\f2\fs26 taskId
\f0\fs24  identifies a specific stateful unit of work. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://a2a-protocol.org/dev/specification/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 A2A Protocol}}\
