\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 Another analogy: Jira\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is actually a useful analogy.\
Think of:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 A2A Context\
\uc0\u8776  Jira Epic / broader work context\
\
A2A Task\
\uc0\u8776  Jira ticket\
\
A2A Message\
\uc0\u8776  comments/messages on the ticket\
\
A2A Artifact\
\uc0\u8776  attachments/deliverables\
\
TaskStatus\
\uc0\u8776  To Do / In Progress / Blocked / Done\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Not exactly technically, but mentally it's quite close.\
You wouldn't identify a Jira issue by the individual comment.\
Likewise:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Message != Task\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 A message may 
\f1\b cause
\f0\b0  a Task to be created.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 Another analogy: HTTP API vs job API\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Consider an ordinary REST API:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 POST /reports\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Response:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \{\
  "report": "..."\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 That's equivalent to:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 A2A Message 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  Message\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 But a long-running API might instead do:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 POST /reports\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Response:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \{\
  "jobId": "job-123",\
  "status": "processing"\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Then:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 GET /jobs/job-123\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 returns:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \{\
  "status": "completed",\
  "result": "report.pdf"\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 A2A Task is conceptually close to that 
\f2\fs26 jobId
\f0\fs24 .\
Except it's standardized for agents and includes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 status lifecycle\
messages\
human input\
authentication interruptions\
artifacts\
streaming\
push notifications\
continuations\
context\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 So:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Task is basically a standardized agent job/workflow primitive.
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 But here's an important nuance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Not every incoming A2A Message creates a Task.\
For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Client:\
"What capabilities do you support?"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Agent could simply answer:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Message:\
"I support architecture review..."\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 No Task necessary.\
A2A explicitly permits the server to return either a stateless 
\f2\fs26 Message
\f0\fs24  for immediate interactions or initiate a stateful 
\f2\fs26 Task
\f0\fs24 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://a2a-protocol.org/dev/topics/life-of-a-task/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 A2A Protocol}}\
Think:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0              Message received\
                    
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2 \
                    
\f3 \uc0\u9660 
\f2 \
          Does this require stateful\
               tracked work?\
                 /      \\\
               NO        YES\
               
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2           
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2 \
               
\f3 \uc0\u9660 
\f2           
\f3 \uc0\u9660 
\f2 \
            Message      Task\
            response      
\f3 \uc0\u9474 
\f2 \
                          
\f3 \uc0\u9660 
\f2 \
                       lifecycle\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

