\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 The one-line definition I would keep\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 An A2A Task is a server-managed, addressable unit of agent work that can live across multiple messages, change state over time, request additional input, and produce artifacts.
\f0\b0 \
Or even shorter:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Message = communication.\
Task = execution.\
Context = continuity.\
Artifact = result.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 That distinction is probably the key concept to understand before going further into A2A.\
}